33	 * starts a follow-up turn. `cancelled`: the turn ended first; `text` is returned to the operator. `rejected`: nothing
34	 * it could steer (a command is running); `text` is returned. `duplicate`: this id was already received. `held`: the
35	 * steering negates a requirement and waits for the operator's decision; the outcome follows as `applied` or `cancelled`.
36	 */
